auth {
  mode: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  Manual testing collection for era-mock-api.

  1. Start the API (`npm run start:dev`) and pick the `local` environment.
  2. Run one of the requests in `Auth` (admin, user or viewer, password `password123`).
     Its post-response script stores the JWT in the `token` environment variable,
     which every other request sends as `Authorization: Bearer {{token}}`.
  3. Create requests save the new id in a runtime variable (e.g. `customerId`)
     that the get / update / delete requests of the same folder use.

  Running the whole collection in order logs in as admin (last login) and leaves the
  data as it was, except for the order status changes; `Seed/Reset` restores everything.
}
